{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789492441,"nonce":"Tp8xUJpUY5deb8R0nJQsiDS/Xyc=","title":"b4 config: b4.searchmask silently ignored since the liblore migration","message":"Problem\n-------\n\nSince db4cd69 (\"Migrate lore access to liblore library\"), no code path in\n``src/b4/`` reads ``b4.searchmask``. Setting it has no effect, and b4 emits\nno warning to say so. A tree-wide grep finds the name only in\n``docs/config.rst``, where it is still documented as a supported setting\nwith a default value.\n\nBefore the migration, ``b4.searchmask`` was the complete query URL\ntemplate: it was applied as ``searchmask % query``, and ``\u0026t=1`` was\nappended to it when full threads were wanted. It could therefore point\nsearches at a host or path entirely unrelated to ``b4.midmask``.\n\nAfter the migration, the search URL is constructed inside liblore from the\nnode's base URL, which b4 derives from ``b4.midmask``. The search endpoint\nis now pinned to the midmask origin, and the query shape is hardcoded.\nliblore's ``from_git_config()`` exposes ``fallback``, ``autoprobe``,\n``probetimeout`` and ``probettl``; there is no search-URL setting for b4 to\npass a ``searchmask`` through to.\n\nImpact\n------\n\nAnyone running on the defaults is unaffected: the pre-migration default\n``https://lore.kernel.org/all/?x=m\u0026q=%s`` is exactly what liblore now\nconstructs. What broke is every *custom* ``b4.searchmask`` -- for example a\nprivate or internal public-inbox whose search endpoint differs from its\nmessage endpoint, or one needing extra query parameters. Those\nconfigurations stopped being honoured without any diagnostic.\n\nThe documented default also advertises ``\u0026t=1``, which is no longer a user\nknob either: liblore decides that parameter from its own ``full_threads``\nargument.\n\nReproduction\n------------\n\nExpected from the code path; not executed as part of this report. With\n``b4.searchmask`` set to an origin different from ``b4.midmask``, any\ncommand that performs a search (for example a trailer update, which queries\nby ``change-id``) should still report ``Grabbing search results from\n\u003cmidmask host\u003e`` and query the midmask origin.\n\nStatus\n------\n\nSurfaced on the list by a patch series that proposed documenting the\nsetting as deprecated. The maintainer's reply identified the ignored\nsetting as a regression rather than an intended deprecation, which is what\nthis report tracks.\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n- Series: https://lore.kernel.org/tools/1789130860.8631fc262581453bbf619ec5b2062170.1a09082676a000c4f3@vates.tech/\n- Maintainer reply: https://lore.kernel.org/tools/20260911-woodoo-pink-barnacle-dbfe65@meerkat/","files":null}]}